{"ts":"2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"b2adadb08f3a0763fd3bf70f","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-l56d0o"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-948: version-skewed pm invocations silently rewrite the tracked merge fence during unrelated commands"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Current and supported older pm versions normalize the managed .gitattributes fence differently, and ordinary commands such as pm health invoke that write path. A read-only diagnostic can therefore dirty a tracked file, weaken extension merge protection, and create unrelated diffs solely from PATH or lockfile version skew. Duplicate evidence: all-status exact GH-948 and title searches returned no match; adjacent merge-guidance and gitattributes ownership items are distinct because they do not own cross-version idempotence or the read-only side-effect boundary."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:merge","area:sdk","determinism","read-only","regression","version-skew"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm health and every read-only bootstrap path leave .gitattributes byte-identical; pm merge install is explicit, deterministic, and preserves compatible managed rules written by newer supported versions; SDK and CLI tests exercise older/newer fence fixtures and dirty-worktree assertions; manual temporary repositories prove health is read-only and explicit installation converges"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-dj98"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"GitHub GH-948"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Node 26.5.0 Linux; @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.3 through 2026.8.9"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run npx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.7 health and @2026.8.9 health against the same initialized tracker, restoring .gitattributes between runs; observe opposing tracked diffs."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Read-only commands never mutate .gitattributes; explicit merge installation is idempotent and preserves compatible newer fence entries across supported version skew; any intentional tracked mutation is reported."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"pm health silently removes or adds managed extension fence lines according to the executing pm version."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.8.3-2026.8.9"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":true},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Agents and contributors accumulate unrelated tracked diffs and can accidentally weaken merge safety when local/global pm versions differ."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-1j5j21","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-tu71","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z","author":"harness:co